  "id": "06-synthesized-enclosing",
  "title": "Synthesized enclosing ranges (scip-php shape): caller attribution is synthesized",
  "rule_pack": "rules-static-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "kind": "synthetic",
    "source": "hand-authored adversarial static case shaped after a scip-php index",
    "seeded_fault": null
  },
  "context": {
    "index": "50d48462d04ff4df4b7e7b02a8dd0c46dd337f27ba91568c3b07f1b45595f6a3"
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "scip-php emits no enclosing ranges; the exporter synthesized them (scip_document.enclosing_synthesized = true, scip_enclosing.synthesized = true) and every edge has caller_synthesized = true.",
    "The positive capability is supported (the path exists) with the discrepancy caller-attribution-synthesized; it is an attribution risk, not a refutation.",
    "Every completeness witness is withheld for synthesized documents, so the authorization gap and the runtime gap both stay unresolved."
  ],
